 "title": "Programming Well: Abstraction and Design in Computation",
 "byline": "Stuart M. Shieber \u00b7 draft textbook for Harvard CS51, \u00a9 2025",
 "note": "PDF page = printed page. The \u201cSupplementary material\u201d notes, problem sets, mathematical background, style guide and exercise solutions at the back are not broken down. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "The textbook for Harvard\u2019s CS51, teaching programming as a design discipline organized around abstraction, using OCaml. It covers expressions and syntax, values and types, naming and scope, functions and currying, structured data and pattern matching, higher-order functions (map, fold, filter), polymorphism, options and exceptions, algebraic and abstract data types with modules and signatures, a substitution-model semantics, complexity and recurrences, mutable state and imperative structures, loops, laziness and streams, objects and inheritance, an environment-model semantics, and concurrency. A final project builds an interpreter for MiniML."
